{"findings":[{"rule_id":"WPS-004","evidence":[{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D12","page":1,"quote":"⌀ 16 H7 (+0.018/0)"},{"kind":"title_block","ref":"surface_treatment","page":1,"quote":"I.Z.B.P. (TRIVALENT)"}],"comment":"The ⌀16 H7 hole (D12) is a tight-tolerance fit feature, but the drawing does not account for the I.Z.B.P. plating thickness specified in the title block. Plating buildup will reduce the finished bore below the H7 limits and prevent assembly with the mating shaft; the designer must either specify masking of the bore or adjust the pre-plate dimension to allow for coating thickness."

  ,
  "recommended_correction": "Add a note specifying that the ⌀16 H7 bore shall be masked during plating, or provide a pre-plate diameter that accounts for the I.Z.B.P. coating thickness so the final size remains within H7 limits."}]}
